{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he shall lay them upon the head of the goat</b>. It is not said regarding the bull of Aaron, nor regarding the sin-offering goat of the Name [designated to HaShem], nor regarding any act of leaning [semikhah] found among the offerings, in this language — because the offerings are for a pleasing odor [reach-toach] upon the fire-offerings of YHWH and they effect favor and atonement. But this one, which is not for the Name [designated to HaShem], and the one receiving it does not effect atonement nor favor — it merely bears their iniquities and answers Amen under compulsion. And when Israel are clean of all sin and transgression, it will bear their sin, as in many verses in the Torah and in the Prophets. And this is: 'and the goat shall bear upon him' [Leviticus 16:22]. And therefore the tongue of crimson wool turns white at the time of the sending of the goat, when it is pushed over the cliff as it is dismembered limb by limb, as is mentioned in the words of the Sages (Yoma 67a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:28.221419827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}